The full text of the Apache License 2.0 follows at the end of this document.


======================================================================
PART B — FLASH Simulation Engine and Derivative Components
======================================================================

flash-sim is an independently developed Python interface and workflow toolkit
for the FLASH radiation-hydrodynamics simulation code. flash-sim is NOT the
FLASH code itself, and is NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by
the Flash Center for Computational Science.

FLASH (the simulation engine) is developed and maintained by the Flash Center
for Computational Science at the University of Rochester. The FLASH code is
governed by its own License Agreement, which ALL users must accept at:

    https://flash.rochester.edu

======================================================================
IMPORTANT — What this package does NOT include
======================================================================

This package DOES NOT include, and therefore does NOT re-distribute:

  - The FLASH source code, compiled binaries, or source tarballs
  - The FLASH SimulationMain example problems (including LaserSlab)
  - The FLASH-distributed EOS/opacity tables (e.g. *.cn4 / *.cnr / *.imx)
  - The FLASH user manual and other FLASH-distributed documentation
  - The IONMIX source code or the MultiEOS data files

None of the above may be re-distributed by individual FLASH users under
Section 3 of the FLASH License Agreement. Users of flash-sim MUST obtain
all of the above independently from the Flash Center's official website
(https://flash.rochester.edu) and accept the FLASH License Agreement
before using flash-sim with a FLASH installation.

======================================================================
Derivative Works — Modified FLASH Example Files (FLASH Agreement §4)
======================================================================

Certain scenario input files under `scenarios/`, `input_gen/*/refs/`, and
related directories are derivative works of FLASH example problem files
(e.g. `Simulation_data.F90`, `Simulation_init.F90`,
`Simulation_initBlock.F90`, `Grid_markRefineDerefine.F90`), modified by
PhySimX Contributors for new physics setups.

In compliance with Section 4 of the FLASH License Agreement:

  (a) Each such file retains a prominent header notice identifying the
      FLASH source file it derives from and stating that the file has been
      modified by PhySimX Contributors. [§4(a) — modifications declared]
  (b) This product includes software developed by and/or derived from the
      Flash Center for Computational Science
      (https://flash.rochester.edu) to which the U.S. Government retains
      certain rights. [§4(b) — acknowledgment displayed]
  (c) The FLASH Code header section describing the origins of the FLASH
      Code and its components remains intact in all modified files.
      [§4(c) — header preserved]

Users re-distributing or further modifying these derivative files must
retain the same notices and acknowledgment.

